# --- bus policies ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A policy file is a list of directives, one per line ("#" starts a comment):
#   bus none                    no session bus at all (the only directive then)
#   include FRAGMENT            the directives of POLICY_DIR/FRAGMENT.inc
#   talk NAME                   only the names in TALK_OK (notifications, the tray, GnuPG's prompter)
#   own NAME                    the application's own names (single instance, MPRIS); NAME or NAME.*
#   call NAME RULE              a portal method call: only the exact (NAME, RULE) pairs in PORTAL_RULES
#   broadcast NAME RULE         a portal signal: the same
#   documents                   bind the document portal's view of this application (file chooser)
#   env SET                     a fixed environment set from ENV_SETS (how a toolkit finds the portal)
#   own-if CONDITION NAME       own NAME only while CONDITION (OWN_IF) holds
#   tray-items                  own org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-<n> (n = 1..TRAY_ITEMS) for the
#                               application's own process id only: Qt 5's tray icon (VLC, KeePassXC)
#                               registers under that name and shows no icon at all if it can't
# Anything else, and any name in FORBIDDEN, makes the application not start (fails closed).
